1c:T46e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Kenya Data Centre Licensing: NFP-T1 and NFP-T2 Explained","description":"Kenya now requires data centre operators to hold an NFP-T2 licence (KES 15M, 15-year term). Here is what the CA's new framework means for operators, investors, and engineers.","url":"https://datacentre254.com/articles/kenya-data-centre-licensing-framework","datePublished":"2026-08-21","dateModified":"2026-08-27","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Kevin Jonathan Onyango Otieno","url":"https://datacentre254.com/about"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Data Centre 254","url":"https://datacentre254.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://datacentre254.com/logo.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://datacentre254.com/articles/kenya-data-centre-licensing-framework"},"articleSection":"Kenya","keywords":"Kenya data centre licensing, NFP-T2 licence Kenya, Communications Authority data centres, Kenya telecoms licensing framework, data centre regulation East Africa, NFP-T1 vs NFP-T2","image":"https://datacentre254.com/images/og-infrastructure-map.webp"}1d:T774,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a colocation data centre need a licence in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Any facility hosting third-party servers requires at minimum an NFP-T2 Network Facilities Provider licence from the Communications Authority. This became explicit under the Revised Telecommunications Market Structure published in March 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the penalty for operating a data centre without a licence?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The CA can issue fines up to KES 300,000 or direct you to cease operations. Under the Kenya Information and Communications Act, operating without a required licence is a regulatory violation that carries both financial penalties and potential enforcement action."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between NFP-T1 and NFP-T2 for data centres?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"NFP-T2 is the primary licence for pure-play data centre operators (KES 15M initial fee, 0.4% AGT or KES 800K annual, 15-year term). NFP-T1 is for large integrated operators who also need nationwide spectrum rights (same initial fee, but 0.4% AGT or KES 4M annual minimum, with an optional 25-year term)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does an existing NFP-T2 licence holder need a new licence to operate a data centre?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Entities that already hold an NFP-T2 licence can establish commercial data centres without any additional authorisation under the updated framework."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many data centres operate in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As of mid-2026, Kenya has 19 operational data centres: 15 in Nairobi and 4 in Mombasa. The market was valued at USD 266 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 805 million by 2031."}}]}13:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen flex flex-col","children":[["$","$L1b",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$1c"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$1d"}}],"$L1e","$L1f"]}],"$L20"]}]
